class Attributes

instance Attributes

instance Method

Instance methods are functions that you define inside a class and can only call on an instance of that class. Just like .__init__(), an instance method always takes self as its first parameter.



When and how to use both - #####

Use class attributes to define properties that should have the same value for every class instance. Use instance attributes for properties that vary from one instance to another.





Encapsulation in Python?

Access modifiers are keywords in object-oriented programming that control which parts of your code can access certain class members, i.e., attributes (or variables) and methods.



